#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119546 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "d5a81b39-421e-55c3-90de-d9f4e6489cd5" :question/math-academy-id "e-4795" :question/problem "Determine if $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2} &= b \\\\\nx_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} + x_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{x_{1} + 5x_{2} = 8; x_{1} + 3x_{2} = 2; 2x_{1} + 2x_{2} =-5\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2} &:=R_{2} - R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3} &:=R_{3} - 2R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2} &:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_{2} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3} &:=R_{3} + 8R_{2} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2} & ↔R_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation\n\n$$\n0x_1 + 0x_2 = 3\n$$\n\nwhich has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2} &= b \\\\\nx_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + x_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\mathbf{b}$ does *not* lie in $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119547 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "94a17888-dcef-58e0-8147-0dec3745f136" :question/math-academy-id "e-4799" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\;\\Pi \\,:\\, \\mathbf{r}=s \\mathbf{b} + t \\mathbf{c}, \\, t,s \\in \\mathbb{R}$, where $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1, 4, 5 \\rangle, \\mathbf{c} = \\langle 2, 4, 6 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{u}= \\langle 2, 10, 12 \\rangle$." :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u} \\in \\Pi$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nsb + tc &= u \\\\\ns\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{s + 2t = 2; 4s + 4t = 10; 5s + 6t = 12\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2} &:=R_{2} - 4R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} - 5R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3} \\mid:=R_{3} - R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{s + 2t = 2; - 4t = 2; 0 = 0\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-4t = 2 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad t = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ns + 2t &= 2 \\\\\ns + 2(-\\frac{1}{2}) &= 2 \\\\\ns - 1 &= 2 \\\\\ns &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution\n\n$$\ns=3, \\, t=-\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $\\Pi$. In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=3\\mathbf{b} - \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{c}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119595 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "21a6808a-5b1c-5b1d-9bd4-da605fb6d920" :question/math-academy-id "e-6218" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2} &= b \\\\\nx_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} + x_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{x_{1} - 2x_{2} = 13; 5x_{1} + 4x_{2} =-5; 7x_{1} + 2x_{2} = k\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2} &:=R_{2} - 5R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} - 7R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k - 91\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2} &:=\\frac{1}{14}R_{2} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k - 91\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} - 16R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k - 11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation\n\n$$\n0x_1 + 0x_2 = k-11\n$$\n\n. Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0 = k-11 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad k=11\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81724303-f879-5db0-9207-e502a59a0ee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117917} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ad45e7-a8bd-52a9-b738-7b95370e7a48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117918} {:answer/id #uuid "b7377951-ec86-5cb6-9370-2c361e7bb68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117919} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e3437a-0176-546f-942b-3d2a88841eee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117920} {:answer/id #uuid "083f23f2-0510-50ba-b8d9-c74088c2c737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b ∉ Span{a_{1}, a_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3e3437a-0176-546f-942b-3d2a88841eee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117920} :answer-field/id #uuid "1173ab11-0849-5c82-b294-bc75dd752ea8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117916}] :question/id #uuid "4d12a13d-137e-5159-9c9a-8fb99c09543c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34205" :question/problem "The vectors $a_{1}$, $a_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b ∈ Span{a_{1}, a_{2}}$. In the affirmative case, find the value of $x_{1} \\cdot x_{2}$ from the decomposition $b = x_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2}$.\n\n$a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}, a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120239 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b58a776-0241-50c0-b9f5-4f9480215e3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117935} {:answer/id #uuid "ce3cfd2f-178e-5550-959f-81ed64858f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117936} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c201c5-1423-508e-8535-384e618ed30b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117937} {:answer/id #uuid "1816acc5-0964-5cf2-9219-a97227a8faa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117938} {:answer/id #uuid "4e2e4b88-69f4-5630-9ef7-89a8da40a766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce3cfd2f-178e-5550-959f-81ed64858f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117936} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ecbaffe-cf4e-5822-809e-5c0fd608abf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117934}] :question/id #uuid "3767254e-f5e7-559c-aca3-b6417b0458c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-34211" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π: r = sb + tc$, $t, s ∈ R$, where $b = ⟨ - 1, 3, 5⟩$, $c = ⟨1,-5,-7⟩$, and $u = ⟨1,-8,-10⟩$. In the affirmative case, find the value of $s \\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u = sb + tc$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fc6d56b-7997-5299-a9d5-42a519af4ccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118204} {:answer/id #uuid "962862f0-7393-53ea-816b-8dbaa9fbec0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118205} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d10058-c774-539a-9141-69e09274e671" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b ∉ Span{a_{1}, a_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118206} {:answer/id #uuid "2c489d3f-d22f-55c9-a088-732fe325d656" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118207} {:answer/id #uuid "33dfc633-8f64-5efe-b764-0666464c6ab8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8d10058-c774-539a-9141-69e09274e671" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b ∉ Span{a_{1}, a_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118206} :answer-field/id #uuid "a96f4c6c-d863-5604-bd96-0e11ca15c1f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118203}] :question/id #uuid "b46516d2-c8a1-53ed-ad0e-7623ea65bae8" :question/math-academy-id "q-34635" :question/problem "The vectors $a_{1}$, $a_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b ∈ Span{a_{1}, a_{2}}$. In the affirmative case, find the value of $x_{1} \\cdot x_{2}$ from the decomposition $b = x_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2}$.\n\n$a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}, a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}$"}]}
